{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You wake up in a maintenance room, alone.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your partner's journal is out in the open.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You probably shouldn't read it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features:</strong> Rachel's Journal is a short (20min) atmospheric reading game. Most of the game is spent reading, and absorbing the vibrant sound design.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Controls:</strong> Mouse-only,\u00a0all actions are performed by left-clicking. Interaction is intuitive and context dependent.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Story:</strong>\u00a0You wake up on a dying colonial vessel, destined for Mars. As one of the few survivors, you're trying to save your failing mission. Unfortunately Rachel's Journal betrays the truth that\u00a0reality is a lot more complicated.\u00a0You're immersed into this world\u00a0with very little context. Sit in your sleeping bag and read as you try to figure out what's really going on.</p>","achievements":{"highlighted":[{"name":"Was that supposed to happen?","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/3890660/81cf947111ff8a8f7f8b806d67942ce85f98853b.jpg"},{"name":"Roll the credits","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/3890660/4f85cd06c3fae9c56cfb049184ee2747318843ff.jpg"},{"name":"The good ending?","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/3890660/e3c5277b82d06f238ab5da1b79775669715cb762.jpg"}],"total":3},"background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3890660?t=1754413524","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3890660?t=1754413524","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3890660/7d6caaa63630824faf107dc7881fcaeef6ec7bb5/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1754413524","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.a